turns:
rust error: cannot borrow `v` as mutable because it is also borrowed as immutable
```rust
let first = &v[0];
v.push(4);
println!("{}", first);
```

light.text:
copy the value out first if you need it later
```rust
let first = v[0];
v.push(4);
println!("{}", first);
```

standard.text:
depends what type is in `v`, but if it implements `Copy` (like an integer) just dereference it:

```rust
let first = v[0];
v.push(4);
println!("{}", first);
```
or if it's not `Copy`, clone it, or just do the push first / print first so the borrow doesn't cross the push

deep.text:
depends on what you need

if you just want to print it, move the print above the push:
```rust
let first = &v[0];
println!("{}", first);
v.push(4);
```
if you actually need it after the push, grab the value instead of a reference (assuming it's a `Copy` type):
```rust
let first = v[0];
v.push(4);
println!("{}", first);
```
